<title>USA: ESC Medical says FDA clears PhotoDerm PL.</title>
<headline>ESC Medical says FDA clears PhotoDerm PL.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israeli medical device maker ESC Medical Systems Ltd said on Monday it received U.S. Food and Drug Administration clearance to market its PhotoDerm PL device.</p>
<p>PhotoDerm PL is an electro-optic device designed for the non-invasive treatment of benign epidermal pigmented lesions and multicolored tattoos by using intense pulsed light.</p>
<p>PhotoDerm PL will be offered as a stand-alone device or as an add-on to PhotoDerm VL, the company said.  PhotoDerm VL, cleared by the FDA in August 1995, is marketed for the treatment of leg veins and other benign vascular lesions.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1733</p>
